+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the site and `npm test` to run the automated WebMCP checks.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The page progressively registers two client-side tools through
+`document.modelContext.registerTool()` in browsers supporting the current
+[WebMCP imperative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+Use a secure context (HTTPS or localhost) and a browser with WebMCP enabled.
+Browsers without that API keep the normal page and links.
+
+| Tool | Input | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get_coffee_shop_info` | `{}` | Reads the current homepage, featured drinks, and supported navigation destinations from the DOM. |
+| `navigate_coffee_shop` | `{"destination":"maple-oat-latte"}` | Clicks the corresponding existing link in the current tab. |
+
+Navigation destinations include `menu`, `locations`, `rewards`, `account`,
+`order-online`, `maple-oat-latte`, `dark-roast-espresso`, `cold-brew`, `about`,
+`careers`, `contact`, and `privacy`. The read tool lists their URLs.
+Logout is not exposed as an agent tool. Navigation accepts only designated,
+same-origin links and validates input at execution time.
+
+The repository contains only the homepage: the linked routes require the same
+hosting/application support as the original navigation links. Opening the order
+page does not place an order. Tools return JSON-serializable values, including
+actionable validation errors. Registration is scoped to the page with
+`AbortSignal` cleanup and restoration on back/forward cache navigation.
+
+Tests run with Node's built-in test runner and a simulated browser API; they do
+not launch a browser or verify native WebMCP implementation behavior.
